      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The Women of Color Resource Center was founded in 1990 by Linda Burnham and Miriam Ching Louie; Burnham served as its Executive Director for 18 years. It includes five objectives: Women’s Human Rights, Popular Education, Welfare, Peace and Justice, and Sisters of Fire. Women of Color Resource Center’s Mission reads:",
